   {
       public DoubleBufferedButton()
       {
           this.DoubleBuffered = true; // Enable double buffering for the button
       }
   }
   ```

4. **Use Custom Buttons**: Replace standard buttons in your custom control with instances of your `DoubleBufferedButton` class.

By following these steps, you should be able to effectively implement double buffering in your custom component with buttons, reducing flickering and improving rendering performance. For more details on enabling double buffering, you can refer to the answer in [How do I enable double-buffering of a control using C# (Windows forms)?](220100).

